RabbitVCS Dolphin VCS plugin
============================

Native Dolphin version-control plugin that integrates RabbitVCS into
Dolphin. It shows the Git/Subversion status of files and adds a
"RabbitVCS Git" / "RabbitVCS SVN" submenu to Dolphin's context menu.

This project is independent of the RabbitVCS source tree; it only needs
the RabbitVCS runtime installed on the system.


Requirements
------------

    * Dolphin / KIO 6, Qt 6 and their development files
    * Extra CMake Modules (ECM), KF6CoreAddons and KF6KIO
    * the RabbitVCS Python package and a `rabbitvcs` launcher in PATH


Build and install
-----------------

    ./scripts/build.sh
    ./scripts/install.sh

Both use /usr as the installation prefix by default. Override it with the
PREFIX environment variable, for example:

    PREFIX=$HOME/.local ./scripts/install.sh

Remove the installed files with:

    ./scripts/uninstall.sh

The plugins are installed into <prefix>/lib/qt6/plugins/dolphin/vcs on a
system prefix; a private prefix is supported as well, in which case Qt needs
to find it through QT_PLUGIN_PATH.


Enable in Dolphin
-----------------

    Settings -> Configure Dolphin... -> Context Menu

Tick "RabbitVCS Git" and/or "RabbitVCS SVN". New version-control plugins are
disabled by default.

Do not enable the stock "Git" or "Subversion" plugin at the same time:
Dolphin picks the first enabled plugin whose marker file (.git / .svn)
matches, so two plugins for the same VCS would compete with each other.


